{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/356127-harry-dresden-lunar-exalted-it-s-canon-or-did-butcher-just-capture-3e-lunars","id":356127,"title":"Harry Dresden, Lunar Exalted (It's canon!) (Or, Did Butcher Just Capture 3e Lunars?)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-31T18:12:31-08:00","id":356127,"title":"Harry Dresden, Lunar Exalted (It's canon!) (Or, Did Butcher Just Capture 3e Lunars?)","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;I have seen many, many newborns, Mr. Dresden. And I can see what they are going to become. You, young shade, are quite simply a monster.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Am not,&quot; I said.<br /> <br /> &quot;Not at the moment, perhaps,&quot; she said. &quot;But... as time goes by, as those you care about grow old and pass on, as you stand helpless while greater events unfold... you will be. Patience.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You're wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> Her dimples deepened. &quot;Why are you so upset, young shade? I really don't see anything with being a monster.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I do,&quot; I said. &quot;The monster part?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh,&quot; the girl said, shaking her head. &quot;Don't be so simple. People adore monsters. They fill their songs and stories with them. They define themselves in relation to them. Do you know what a monster is, young shade? Power. Power and choice. Monsters make choices. Monsters shape the world. Monsters force us to become strong, smarter, better. They sift the weak from the strong and provide a forge for the steeling of souls. Even as we curse monsters, we admire them. Seek to become them, in some ways.&quot; Her eyes became distant. &quot;There are far, far worse things to be than a monster.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Monsters hurt people. I don't.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> &quot;I crossed a line,&quot; I said quietly. &quot;Lines, plural. I did things I shouldn't have done. It wasn't right. And I knew it. But... I wanted to help the little girl. And I...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sinned?&quot; she suggested, her large eyes eerily serene. &quot;Chose the left-hand path? Fell from grace? Cast the world into madness?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Whatever,&quot; I said.<br /> <br /> &quot;And you think you aren't a monster.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Dresden being a Lunar or not aside, do you think the girl's speech on what a monster is capture the spirit of what next edition Lunar's have been presented as so far?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T18:23:38-08:00","id":356151,"title":"","content":"I've always thought of Mr. Harry Blackfield Coperstone Dresden(Conjure it at your own risk) as a particularly Sorcery focused Slayer, but the quote does seem to harken to what I've heard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T18:32:57-08:00","id":356159,"title":"","content":"Man I love that conversation but I am a sucker for the all or nothing sacrifice for something that means more than life and morality and honor. That said I do think the role of monster is one that lunars do very well, that said aside from the body horror and ability to disconnect from just about everything the role is not just theirs. I mean you can do the role quite well with abyssals as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T18:33:35-08:00","id":356161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/356127-harry-dresden-lunar-exalted-it-s-canon-or-did-butcher-just-capture-3e-lunars?p=356151#post356151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always thought of Mr. Harry Blackfield Coperstone Dresden(Conjure it at your own risk) as a particularly Sorcery focused Slayer, but the quote does seem to harken to what I've heard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slayers and other Infernals have some claim to the word &quot;monster&quot;. As do Abyssals, Liminals, possibly Getimians, and any Exalt who cares not one whit for the people he tramples underfoot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T19:05:54-08:00","id":356171,"title":"","content":"I see Lunars as more looking like monsters, having the feel of fantasy monsters (big, scary, claws, etc), rather than being defined as moral monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T21:03:06-08:00","id":356209,"title":"","content":"To have power and choice is the definition of being Exalted, regardless of form.<br /> <br /> That quote doesn't really apply to any type of Exalt in particular. Though one could actually make an argument that it is the furthest from Lunars because they can become more like animals in form, they run the chance of thinking like them. This in turn means they wouldn't see things in such flowerly terms as &quot;monster&quot;, &quot;Good&quot;, &quot;Evil&quot;, or even &quot;Sin&quot;.<br /> <br /> An animal treats things in a more relevant sense, is something dangerous, is something required to survive, is something enjoyable, etc. Most of it almost breaks down to a &quot;If Then&quot; style of logic.<br /> <br /> Any attempt to put human style thinking about morals, ethics, sin or monstrosity into the animal world is just kind of silly in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T21:26:53-08:00","id":356240,"title":"","content":"If anybody is a lunar It's Listens-to-winds aka Injun-Joe, and now that I think of it Shagnasty makes for a pretty good Chimera too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T23:22:08-08:00","id":356316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/356127-harry-dresden-lunar-exalted-it-s-canon-or-did-butcher-just-capture-3e-lunars?p=356161#post356161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slayers and other Infernals have some claim to the word &amp;quot;monster&amp;quot;. As do Abyssals, Liminals, possibly Getimians, and any Exalt who cares not one whit for the people he tramples underfoot.</div> </div> </div> </div> In all honesty, I didn't chose Slayer because of the quote; it's more because he seems to embody a Malfean sort of theme: power unrelenting, endurance, and 